         <occupation>Barrister</occupation>
         <note type="editorial">
            <p>Charles William Edward Jerningham was the son of Edward Jerningham and Emily Middleton. He lived in Painswick, Gloucestershire, though he often spent time in London due to his work as a barrister. In September 1841, he married Emma Mary Wynn Roberts and the pair had 5 children. </p>
            <p>A surviving letter from <persName xml:id="SHE02">Mary Wollstonecraft Shelley</persName> records her invitation to Charles Jerningham for “a small evening party” on 7 June 1830, which Godwin also attended. Although there are earlier references to a Jerningham before 1812 (coded as the actor and poet <persName xml:id="JER01">Edward Jerningham</persName>) the entries between 1829 and 1831 seem to reference different individual. This later Jerningham, with who Godwin had a closer relationship, is likely to be Charles Jerningham.  </p>
         </note>
